<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bückeburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bückeburg is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steinhuder-meer">Steinhuder Meer</a>. Count Ernst of Holstein-Schaumburg made it his residence in the early 17th century and rebuilt its palace and church, and from 1647 to 1946 it was the capital of Schaumburg-Lippe. The princely family still lives in the palace.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/buckeburg.jpg" alt="Bückeburg" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Klaus-Big · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blick_zur_Stadtkirche.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
